Derived from QEMU 1:7.2+dfsg-7+deb12u18, softmmu/icount.c, accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops-icount.c

Subject: icount: do not warp QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL over an unaccounted vCPU slice

icount_start_warp_timer() runs in the main loop (main_loop_wait, timerlist_rearm) and
advances qemu_icount_bias by the distance to the next QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL deadline when
all vCPUs are idle. The main thread has current_cpu == NULL, so QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL there
is qemu_icount as of the last icount_process_data(). Between a vCPU executing HLT
(halted = 1, so "idle") and icount_process_data() accounting that slice, the clock lags
by the slice's instructions, the computed deadline is too large and the warp overshoots.
Whether the main loop wakes inside that window depends on host scheduling, so two runs
of the same guest diverge by a few ms of guest time under host load.

Skip the warp while any vCPU slice is unaccounted (icount_budget != 0). The vCPU thread
notifies the main loop after accounting when all CPUs are idle (rr_cpu_thread_fn), so the
warp then happens with an exact clock.
--- a/softmmu/icount.c
+++ b/softmmu/icount.c
@@ -310,6 +310,16 @@
     if (replay_mode != REPLAY_MODE_PLAY) {
         if (!all_cpu_threads_idle()) {
             return;
+        }
+
+        {
+            CPUState *cs;
+            CPU_FOREACH(cs) {
+                if (qatomic_load_acquire(&cs->icount_budget) != 0) {
+                    /* slice not yet accounted: the clock lags, see header */
+                    return;
+                }
+            }
         }
 
         if (qtest_enabled()) {
--- a/accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops-icount.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/tcg-accel-ops-icount.c
@@ -127,7 +127,7 @@
     /* Reset the counters */
     cpu_neg(cpu)->icount_decr.u16.low = 0;
     cpu->icount_extra = 0;
-    cpu->icount_budget = 0;
+    qatomic_store_release(&cpu->icount_budget, 0);
 
     replay_account_executed_instructions();
 
